  "term": "Zarontin",
  "definition": "Zarontin is an anticonvulsant succinimide drug used to help prevent seizures. Its action is not fully understood, but it is thought to partly block T-type calcium channels in thalamic neurons, reducing abnormal burst firing and helping stabilize brain nerve activity.",
